                "text": "### 🏛️ Window Width Updates and Model Inspection\n\nAll eight pavilion windows have been widened from 1,500 mm to 1,800 mm while maintaining their centred wall positions, preserving all entity IDs, wall attachments, heights, sill heights, the ground floor door, slabs, storeys, and flat roof.\n\n---\n\n### 📋 Changed Entities\n\nEach modified opening retained its stable identifier, host wall association, sill height (900 mm), and height (1,500 mm), with its width updated to 1,800 mm:\n\n* **`e08536cf-2375-462a-b6c1-216f1a8b0945` (`W-G-01`)**\n  * Level: Ground\n  * Host Wall: `6bce9a7b-abdb-44e0-918a-64057c51cf46` (Ground South Wall, length 12,000 mm)\n  * Offset: 6,000 mm (centred)\n  * Dimensions: 1,800 mm wide × 1,500 mm high (sill 900 mm)\n* **`712b5a48-8c2e-4cbc-a860-7c093baa59a1` (`W-G-02`)**\n  * Level: Ground\n  * Host Wall: `6fb2662f-c56c-4a16-90c8-a1d4a2c7a66c` (Ground East Wall, length 8,000 mm)\n  * Offset: 4,000 mm (centred)\n  * Dimensions: 1,800 mm wide × 1,500 mm high (sill 900 mm)\n* **`6695253b-e0f4-4f34-87a0-610bd5a363ce` (`W-G-03`)**\n  * Level: Ground\n  * Host Wall: `38b8617b-9944-479d-95f0-b4bb6cf4492b` (Ground North Wall, length 12,000 mm)\n  * Offset: 6,000 mm (centred)\n  * Dimensions: 1,800 mm wide × 1,500 mm high (sill 900 mm)\n* **`63d78ae1-d4fe-4e73-bc6e-ff6de8ca33da` (`W-G-04`)**\n  * Level: Ground\n  * Host Wall: `fcb37c1f-a878-4386-bd70-68fcc3a207d1` (Ground West Wall, length 8,000 mm)\n  * Offset: 4,000 mm (centred)\n  * Dimensions: 1,800 mm wide × 1,500 mm high (sill 900 mm)\n* **`481f79a5-f81b-4669-b0c3-771eef27406d` (`W-U-01`)**\n  * Level: Upper Level\n  * Host Wall: `b1c219dd-2f43-4e74-bce1-e06d0a9935a1` (Upper South Wall, length 12,000 mm)\n  * Offset: 6,000 mm (centred)\n  * Dimensions: 1,800 mm wide × 1,500 mm high (sill 900 mm)\n* **`08a1cb1f-b2a5-4ef7-a1cc-4b0826aff3d6` (`W-U-02`)**\n  * Level: Upper Level\n  * Host Wall: `a039c525-e70c-4239-8a41-3b3b16960cb3` (Upper East Wall, length 8,000 mm)\n  * Offset: 4,000 mm (centred)\n  * Dimensions: 1,800 mm wide × 1,500 mm high (sill 900 mm)\n* **`4f367a06-223c-4669-ab3d-78e1317d829a` (`W-U-03`)**\n  * Level: Upper Level\n  * Host Wall: `e0b51709-e201-4d6c-b47f-279eec8a0b41` (Upper North Wall, length 12,000 mm)\n  * Offset: 6,000 mm (centred)\n  * Dimensions: 1,800 mm wide × 1,500 mm high (sill 900 mm)\n* **`da190670-2d18-4231-a0f3-a8d1328631cf` (`W-U-04`)**\n  * Level: Upper Level\n  * Host Wall: `149c5af6-d2b9-48ab-aab4-e04fc5bcccc5` (Upper West Wall, length 8,000 mm)\n  * Offset: 4,000 mm (centred)\n  * Dimensions: 1,800 mm wide × 1,500 mm high (sill 900 mm)\n\n---\n\n### 📐 Preserved Geometry & Current Totals\n\n* **Door `397c05f1-72ec-47ef-a543-52d75fd19fa4` (`D-01`)**: Unchanged at 1,200 mm wide × 2,400 mm high, offset 2,000 mm along Ground South Wall.\n* **Storey Levels (2)**: Ground (`8a76bc99-312a-4f9a-8dd5-08515e2bf913`) at 0 mm elevation, Upper Level (`4676f1a3-0167-4934-8425-4fdc333d3c08`) at 3,600 mm elevation (each 3,600 mm storey height).\n* **Walls (8)**: 4 ground walls and 4 upper walls intact.\n* **Floor Slabs (2)**: Ground slab (`2c12097b-96fc-4cdb-a933-b0f78c127101`) and upper slab (`bac7669b-901f-42f6-9845-62bdff58252a`), both 250 mm thick concrete spanning the 12 m × 8 m footprint.\n* **Roof (1)**: Flat roof (`63bb0393-d3e6-40da-a763-c555d58e2883`) at 7,200 mm overall height (offset 3,600 mm above Upper Level) with zero eaves.\n* **Openings Total**: 9 (8 windows, 1 door).\n* **Design Revision**: Revision 4 saved and readback-verified.\n\n---\n\n### 🔍 Visual Inspection & Limitations\n\n```mindmap\nPavilion Design Revision 4\n  Status: Illustrative Conceptual Draft\n  Evidence State: Inferred Geometry\n  Scope: Internal Review Only\n  Verification: Uncalibrated, Non-Certified\n```\n\n* **Visual Check**: The solid 3D canvas capture confirms that the two-storey massing, planar parapet edge, exterior wall alignments, and wider 1.8 m window apertures are properly generated without mesh intersecting or displaced frames.\n* **Evidence Limits**: This pavilion is an internal conceptual wireframe model. All components carry an **inferred** evidence state; they are not derived from calibrated source drawings and do not constitute structural, thermal, egress, or construction compliance documentation.",
